zΔ⚡b|=1739|-2|+The|=24|+ starts with the same two%2Dline [[header]] as the context format|=3|+xcept th|=1|+t the original file is pre|=1|+eded by '%2D%2D%2D' and t|=1|+e|=1|+new fi|=1|+e is preceded by '%2B%2B%2B'.%0A%0AFollow|=2|+g this ar|=2|+a number of 'change hunks' (chunks) |=5|+c|=1|+ntain information on how the original file must be |=1|+hanged to obtain the new file.%0A%0AA |=1|+h|=1|+nk begins with |=1|+ange information (contained on 1 line) and i|=2|+immediately foll|=1|+wed by a |=1|+umber of |=1|-1|+ines|=1|+provid|=2|+g|=1|+con|=1|-1|=1|+xtual,|=1|+addition or deletion in|=1|+ormat|=1|+on. Contextual lines a|=1|+e preceded by a |=1|+pace (' '), addi|=1|+ion|=1|-1|+l|=1|+nes are preceded by a plus ('%2B'), and de|=2|+tion|=1|+l|=1|+ne|=1|+ are|=15|+('%2D').%0A%0AAddition line|=1|+ are ones that should be added to the or|=2|+i|=1|-1|+al|=1|+fil|=1|+ to obt|=1|-1|+in t|=1|+e new|=1|+fi|=1|+e.%0ADelet|=1|+o|=1|+ lines ar|=2|+ones |=5|+sh|=1|-1|+uld be deleted from the original file to obtain the new file.%0A%0AThe |=1|+ontext|=1|+al lines a|=1|+e optional, but generally |=1|+urround the|=1|+additi|=2|+ and/or deletion lines, traditional|=3|+3 at the beg|=2|+ning and 3 at|=5|+end of each chunk.%0AThe|=2|+ are lines that have not |=1|-1|+ha|=1|+ge|=2|+between the two |=4|+s,|=1|-1|+and so can be used as a reference to locate the chunk'|=3|+lace in the file. P|=1|+oviding cont|=1|+xt with su|=1|+h lin|=1|+s is useful both for human [[rea|=1|+ability]] & r|=1|+ference, an|=2|-1|+for an|=2|+[[p|=1|+tch]]|=2|+rogram trying to app|=1|-1|+y |=1|+aid diff to a|=2|+l|=2|+htly modified versio|=1|+ of the original file. If|=2|+s|=1|+y, li|=1|+es have been inserte|=2|+before a |=1|+hunk in the |=1|+riginal file, the chunkrange's [[line nu|=1|-1|+ber]]s (see below) will likely be incorrect, yet the c|=2|+textual|=7|+m|=1|-1|+y allow th|=3|+atch p|=1|+ogram to find th|=1|+ |=1|+orr|=1|+ct location to ad|=1|+/r|=1|+move the chunk's lines. If two chunks occur very close to